00:17:10.750 --> 00:17:13.620
Miss Rei Aragaki.

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:21.080
Oh! You're one of the agents
who was chasing Leo!

00:17:21.080 --> 00:17:24.290
Yes. I work with him.

00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:25.700
Why...?

00:17:25.700 --> 00:17:30.580
Will you come with me for
a moment? It's about Leonardo.

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:48.950
I'll lure his chaperone away, so go into
the room when you find an opening.

00:17:48.950 --> 00:17:51.200
He's in that room.

00:17:51.200 --> 00:17:54.330
Um, why are you doing this...?

00:17:54.330 --> 00:17:58.580
Do you know what he was called in England?

00:17:58.580 --> 00:18:02.870
Huh? Um, the "pride of Royal"?

00:18:02.870 --> 00:18:04.700
That's right.

00:18:04.700 --> 00:18:10.700
The young genius everyone acknowledged,
even in a top ballet company.

00:18:10.700 --> 00:18:15.290
Because of that brilliant talent, he ran away.

00:18:15.290 --> 00:18:16.540
Huh?

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:22.410
Sometimes, expectation can be a heavy burden.

00:18:22.410 --> 00:18:26.700
Just because someone is a genius doesn't
mean that they are mentally strong.

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:29.750
Leo...

00:18:29.750 --> 00:18:34.250
My job is to take him back
to the ballet company.

00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:41.330
But... I don't think he could stand on
stage again if I bring him back now.

00:18:41.330 --> 00:18:45.830
He might even quit dancing.

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:52.830
That would mean I failed at my job, right?
That's why I went to get you.

00:18:52.830 --> 00:18:56.870
You're worried about Leo, aren't you?

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:02.790
Enter the room in five minutes.

00:19:13.750 --> 00:19:17.290
So this is where you were, Leo.

00:19:19.290 --> 00:19:25.080
Dad's competition was today, you know.
I was waiting for you the whole time at the--

00:19:25.080 --> 00:19:28.910
Don't just stand there. Have a seat first.

00:19:28.910 --> 00:19:32.040
Huh? R-Right...

00:19:33.290 --> 00:19:34.870
Sorry.

00:19:34.870 --> 00:19:37.200
For leaving without saying anything.

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:40.370
That's... okay.

00:19:40.370 --> 00:19:42.830
I decided to go back to England.

00:19:42.830 --> 00:19:45.410
So I could go back to the ballet company.

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:49.620
G-Go back?! B-But that's
the ballet company you--

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:51.200
Ran away from?

00:19:52.660 --> 00:19:54.200
That's true.

00:19:54.200 --> 00:19:56.910
Th-Then--

00:19:56.910 --> 00:19:59.200
It's thanks to you guys.

00:19:59.200 --> 00:20:03.330
My life here helped me get back on my feet.

00:20:03.330 --> 00:20:07.790
"I want to dance again."
It made me able to feel that way.

00:20:07.790 --> 00:20:09.700
I'm truly grateful.

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:18.080
Even so... you should watch
Dad's gymnastics before you go.

00:20:18.080 --> 00:20:25.700
Dad believes that you'll go see him, you know!
He said he wanted to show you his gymnastics!

00:20:30.580 --> 00:20:34.620
Joe has to do what he has to do,
and I have to do what I have to do.

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:36.040
Huh?

00:20:37.330 --> 00:20:41.410
Or do you think I should
go watch Joe's gymnastics

00:20:41.410 --> 00:20:44.330
even if it means abandoning
what I should be doing?

00:20:44.330 --> 00:20:45.830
That's...

00:20:45.830 --> 00:20:47.410
"That's"?

00:20:51.580 --> 00:20:54.660
I'll write once I'm back in England.

00:20:54.660 --> 00:20:57.160
I'm glad I got to see you one last time.

00:20:57.160 --> 00:20:59.620
Take care, Rei.

00:21:17.370 --> 00:21:20.370
Goodbye, Joe...
